WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.360
In Matthew's Gospel,
Jesus tells his followers:

2
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:07.470
your Father knows what things
you need before you ask him.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.310
Then, a few lines later, he
gives them a prayer to say.

4
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.020
Today, that prayer is said by
Christians of almost every denomination.

5
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.270
So if God already knows what you
need, why do Christians pray at all?

6
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.300
In this mission, you'll sort
prayers into four types,

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.360
and take the Lord's
Prayer apart line by line.

8
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:32.430
Then you'll weigh up whether set prayers
are more valuable than informal prayer.

9
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.530
Your mission: find out
why Christians pray,

10
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.800
if God already knows what they need.
